From 817fa09f4910535725671889236bdcb10ddd04b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 02:09:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] plugin: add registry support

Add a registry used to associate plugin interfaces with
plugin factories.

The registry provides the lookup mechanism used by the
plugin framework to locate factories responsible for
creating runtime plugin instances.

Add support for builtin plugin registration. Builtin
registration serves as the framework composition point
for integrating plugin implementations compiled into
phosphor-logging.

Separating plugin lookup from plugin construction keeps
plugin-specific logic encapsulated within PluginFactory
implementations and out of framework consumers.

Registering the same plugin interface more than once is
treated as an error, ensuring a one-to-one mapping
between plugin interfaces and factory implementations.

Add unit tests covering plugin registration and factory
lookup. Update Meson build files to build the registry
implementation and associated test cases. Also update
OpenPOWER PEL test configuration to accommodate the new
plugin test infrastructure.

No runtime plugin processing is introduced by this
change.

Change-Id: Ib48a62ed323ef0181595e9c9f53e5227792d1dc4
Signed-off-by: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
